From: Motion Browser Fork Maintainers <motion@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 21 Feb 2025 10:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 0001] motion: branding — product name
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Purpose
=======
Rebrand the browser surface strings from the Chromium default to the Motion
Browser fork identity: `app_name` (launcher/activity label) becomes
"Motion Browser", and a `motion_product_name` string is added for
Motion-specific UI to reference instead of hardcoding.

Rebase notes
============
- The exact string file may shift between revisions: upstream splits or moves
  per-channel name strings (channel_constants.xml has gained channel variants
  and brand-specific copies in the past). If the anchor below no longer
  matches, locate the equivalent product-name string resource for the
  chrome_public_apk target and re-shape this hunk minimally.
- tools/apply_patches.sh tolerates this drift: it applies via `git am --3way`,
  falls back to `git apply --3way`, and finally to `patch --fuzz=3` when
  MOTION_PATCH_ALLOW_FUZZ=1 (default).
- Do NOT translate `motion_product_name`; it is a fork identity constant.

Honesty note (spec §77)
=======================
Authored against the upstream file layout as documented for 130.0.6723.58.
NOT verified against a real Chromium checkout — rebase expected.
---
 chrome/android/java/res/values/channel_constants.xml | 9 +++++++--
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/chrome/android/java/res/values/channel_constants.xml b/chrome/android/java/res/values/channel_constants.xml
index 1a2b3c4d..5e6f7a8b 100644
--- a/chrome/android/java/res/values/channel_constants.xml
+++ b/chrome/android/java/res/values/channel_constants.xml
@@ -4,6 +4,11 @@
      found in the LICENSE file. -->
 
 <resources>
-    <!-- The application name displayed to the user. -->
-    <string name="app_name" translateable="false">Chromium</string>
+    <!-- The application name displayed to the user.
+         Motion (0001): fork product branding. The exact string file shifts
+         between Chromium revisions (channel variants may be split into other
+         values/ files); apply_patches.sh tolerates that drift via 3-way and
+         fuzz fallback. -->
+    <string name="app_name" translateable="false">Motion Browser</string>
+    <string name="motion_product_name" translateable="false">Motion Browser</string>
 </resources>
